From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patryk <papyszoo@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 19:00:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PS5: BetterVR in PS5-ECAM's own ELF, over the OpenXR runtime
 on hmd2

BotW-BetterVR on PS5 (M3). Built with the PS5 SDK's clang 18 and libc++ 18 into one object the app
links (port/bettervr/layer); the app supplies the Vulkan loader's part and the OpenXR runtime.

- Cemu's three exports named directly (no dynamic linker); whether the layer acts is the app's
  switch (BetterVR_PS5_LayerWanted)
- one lock (ps5xr::QueueMutex) around every submission and present on the console's one graphics queue
- RND_Renderer::EndSession for the Linux renderer (renderer.cpp, which had it, is Windows-only)
- libc++ 18: generic formatter contexts, strtod for floats (no floating-point std::from_chars)
- no sys/sysinfo.h, no browser to open links in, no signal to end the process with
